\frametitle{Curriculum platform scope: not an inference engine or hosted LMS}

The curriculum is deliberately broad (630 skills across all eight
strata) and designed so that growth is a data operation: adding skills
or worked examples extends the catalog without changing the engine. Its
new practice layer is still pedagogical rather than clinical or
operational advice: domain-fit, ethics, misuse, and evaluation skills
train learners to ask better modeling questions, not to deploy
autonomous interventions without local review. Out of scope for this
release are hosting and authentication of a production SkillTree
deployment, learner analytics, and a textbook-length treatment of every
individual skill. The local dashboard narrows that boundary: it is
enough to show that the export can be inspected locally and, when a
SkillTree runtime is available, opened through subject and quiz routes;
it is not a hosted LMS or analytics product.
